1
00:00:22,105 --> 00:00:23,815
Does this look okay?

2
00:00:26,609 --> 00:00:29,195
It doesn't look weird, does it?

3
00:00:37,370 --> 00:00:40,999
Today, I'm going on
my first date with Kazehaya.

4
00:00:42,167 --> 00:00:47,005
On that note, this skirt
feels a little shorter than I expected.

5
00:00:48,673 --> 00:00:49,966
I hope this is okay.

6
00:00:51,551 --> 00:00:53,678
Please, no mistakes today.

7
00:01:01,436 --> 00:01:05,315
I... I kept you waiting again. I'm sorry.

8
00:01:08,234 --> 00:01:11,488
You're good. I just figured
I'd show up here a little bit early.

9
00:01:11,571 --> 00:01:12,906
That was my decision.

10
00:01:12,989 --> 00:01:15,742
Nothin' like a bunch'a nerves
to get you outta bed early!

11
00:01:15,825 --> 00:01:18,078
- Tha-- that was me too!
- Really?

12
00:01:18,161 --> 00:01:19,496
Uh, uh-huh.

13
00:01:20,997 --> 00:01:22,707
That's cool!

14
00:01:26,503 --> 00:01:28,463
Whoa!

15
00:01:30,799 --> 00:01:33,218
- Can I have some?
- Mmm.

16
00:01:41,518 --> 00:01:42,519
It's so good.

17
00:01:42,602 --> 00:01:44,729
Uh-oh.

18
00:01:44,813 --> 00:01:48,441
- Oh.
- Darn it. Here come the happy tears.

19
00:01:50,068 --> 00:01:54,489
Today,
is a day I'll never forget.

20
00:02:02,455 --> 00:02:05,375
- Mmm, actually...
- Hmm?

21
00:02:07,085 --> 00:02:10,130
I wish you a very happy birthday!

22
00:02:10,964 --> 00:02:12,465
Huh? Wha--

23
00:02:13,049 --> 00:02:14,300
It's your birthday.

24
00:02:15,301 --> 00:02:17,929
Truth is, I feel terrible saying this,

25
00:02:18,012 --> 00:02:21,266
but I only found out a few days ago
that today is your birthday.

26
00:02:21,808 --> 00:02:24,602
Please forgive me
for not planning a celebration.

27
00:02:24,686 --> 00:02:26,938
Wait. It's fine. Really!

28
00:02:27,522 --> 00:02:32,652
I know it's a little late,
but... I did manage to find you a present.

29
00:02:33,820 --> 00:02:36,656
It would make me
really happy if you accepted it.

30
00:02:37,157 --> 00:02:38,867
Y-- you mean it?

31
00:02:40,243 --> 00:02:41,327
Here.

32
00:02:42,412 --> 00:02:45,373
I hope you and Maru
will have lots of fun with this toy.

33
00:02:45,456 --> 00:02:47,167
Whoa! Thank you.

34
00:02:48,793 --> 00:02:53,089
And this too.
May it bring lots of joy to you and Maru.

35
00:02:53,173 --> 00:02:56,926
- Huh? Two toys?
- Nice!

36
00:02:57,510 --> 00:02:59,179
And there's also this.

37
00:02:59,262 --> 00:03:01,681
I thought you and Maru
might find this enjoyable.

38
00:03:01,764 --> 00:03:03,892
Thank you.

39
00:03:04,893 --> 00:03:06,728
Now that I think about it,

40
00:03:06,811 --> 00:03:09,981
I might've accidentally gotten
more birthday presents for Maru

41
00:03:10,064 --> 00:03:11,900
than for Kazehaya.

42
00:03:12,901 --> 00:03:15,528
- Here.
- Hm? What's this?

43
00:03:23,912 --> 00:03:27,332
I really loved
the cellphone strap you gave me that day.

44
00:03:39,427 --> 00:03:43,181
Uh, thanks a lot. I appreciate it.

45
00:03:43,806 --> 00:03:46,976
Funny story about that strap.

46
00:03:47,602 --> 00:03:49,646
How I went out and bought it
on the same day I heard

47
00:03:49,729 --> 00:03:52,482
you couldn't make it
to the Christmas party we all had.

48
00:03:53,608 --> 00:03:56,527
I know you must have felt
really upset about that.

49
00:03:56,611 --> 00:03:57,946
Sorry I couldn't help.

50
00:03:58,655 --> 00:04:00,782
I wanted to get you something though.

51
00:04:02,242 --> 00:04:06,788
Not just for the class present exchange
but a gift for you specifically.

52
00:04:08,414 --> 00:04:11,167
When I saw the strap,
it reminded me of you.

53
00:04:11,251 --> 00:04:12,794
So I got it.

54
00:04:17,340 --> 00:04:18,466
Thank you for this.

55
00:04:19,467 --> 00:04:20,551
I'll cherish it.

56
00:04:23,638 --> 00:04:27,809
What do I do?
I was hoping it would make him happy.

57
00:04:29,727 --> 00:04:32,689
But... I'm the one who's happy.

58
00:05:02,510 --> 00:05:05,179
- Why don't we sit here?
- Okay.

59
00:05:06,014 --> 00:05:07,473
It's pretty empty.

60
00:05:07,557 --> 00:05:09,976
- Why not put that on a chair?
- Y-- yeah.

61
00:05:10,977 --> 00:05:14,480
That's cool.
The seats here recline.

62
00:05:14,564 --> 00:05:16,274
Yeah, it's not like the movies.

63
00:05:32,665 --> 00:05:35,251
I'm really happy.

64
00:05:54,228 --> 00:05:59,067
Well, first star's out.
That's Lyra's... Vega? I think?

65
00:05:59,150 --> 00:06:01,069
Some say "Orihime."

66
00:06:01,778 --> 00:06:04,238
Vega's a magnitude zero star, isn't it?

67
00:06:04,322 --> 00:06:07,325
Better keep your eyes
on the road, or you'll trip!

68
00:06:08,159 --> 00:06:10,828
Yeah.

69
00:06:32,683 --> 00:06:35,228
Um... thanks for that.

70
00:06:52,120 --> 00:06:53,079
Wait.

71
00:06:56,249 --> 00:07:00,169
- Mm?
- Could we... talk a bit?

72
00:07:11,347 --> 00:07:13,808
Honestly... I wasn't sure

73
00:07:13,891 --> 00:07:16,686
whether it was a good idea
to give this to you.

74
00:07:17,937 --> 00:07:23,192
It's not exactly the right season
for this, and it's a bit unwieldy.

75
00:07:24,068 --> 00:07:26,362
I really hope this isn't too much trouble.

76
00:07:29,532 --> 00:07:30,533
Oh.

77
00:07:31,117 --> 00:07:34,954
It's the hat I was going to
give you for Christmas but couldn't.

78
00:07:36,164 --> 00:07:39,459
My dad got it.
I know it was an honest mistake,

79
00:07:39,542 --> 00:07:42,503
but I... I knitted it just for you.

80
00:07:44,755 --> 00:07:48,050
I know this must look like
I'm just giving you my dad's hat...

81
00:07:48,885 --> 00:07:51,304
You don't have to wear it
if you don't want to.

82
00:07:51,888 --> 00:07:54,056
- I also...
- Hm?

83
00:07:54,932 --> 00:07:58,102
I brought the chocolates I couldn't
give you on Valentine's Day.

84
00:07:59,395 --> 00:08:02,398
I made sure yours had a bit more chocolate
than the others.

85
00:08:04,692 --> 00:08:07,653
But I was too scared to give it to you.

86
00:08:10,823 --> 00:08:16,287
These are the presents I had always wanted
to give to you... but never could.

87
00:08:23,127 --> 00:08:24,962
That's really good!

88
00:08:25,546 --> 00:08:27,965
I'm... so happy!

89
00:08:31,052 --> 00:08:35,598
I... I still don't know
what a girlfriend's job really is, but...

90
00:08:36,098 --> 00:08:36,974
Kuronuma.

91
00:08:38,142 --> 00:08:39,310
It's not a job.

92
00:08:39,977 --> 00:08:41,354
It really isn't.

93
00:08:42,480 --> 00:08:44,315
You just gotta be yourself.

94
00:08:46,192 --> 00:08:48,236
Am I contradicting myself?

95
00:08:48,736 --> 00:08:50,196
I'm so happy!

96
00:08:50,279 --> 00:08:55,076
So happy that I wish...
time would just hurry and fly right by us.

97
00:08:55,910 --> 00:09:00,540
So that... being together with you
all the time can finally feel normal.

98
00:09:07,046 --> 00:09:08,881
But that would be such a waste.

99
00:09:09,632 --> 00:09:12,426
I couldn't do that.

100
00:09:13,010 --> 00:09:16,973
Sorry, I thought I was the only one
who felt this way.

101
00:09:18,641 --> 00:09:20,393
I'm so happy.

102
00:09:22,311 --> 00:09:23,563
Kazehaya said

103
00:09:25,106 --> 00:09:27,358
he feels the same way that I do.

104
00:09:41,789 --> 00:09:48,129
FROM ME TO YOU: KIMI NI TODOKE
3RD SEASON

105
00:10:38,054 --> 00:10:42,975
EPISODE 1
THERE'S NO WAY I WOULD HATE YOU

106
00:10:44,602 --> 00:10:47,980
Summer is a time
rife with temptations.

107
00:10:49,190 --> 00:10:51,567
Many excitements will assail you.

108
00:10:52,568 --> 00:10:55,780
But as a student,
your job is to stay focused!

109
00:10:56,572 --> 00:11:00,326
Summer vacation is not an excuse
to get carried away.

110
00:11:01,243 --> 00:11:04,872
So remember
to conduct yourselves with propriety.

111
00:11:05,915 --> 00:11:08,751
It's finally summer!

112
00:11:08,834 --> 00:11:11,253
- We're on vacation!
- Yeah!

113
00:11:14,006 --> 00:11:15,549
What are you so excited about?!

114
00:11:15,633 --> 00:11:17,885
Weren't any of you listening?!

115
00:11:17,968 --> 00:11:20,763
Excitement is the enemy here!
It'll trip you up!

116
00:11:21,263 --> 00:11:24,684
As a student, your duty is to

117
00:11:25,726 --> 00:11:27,353
focus on your studies.

118
00:11:28,813 --> 00:11:30,356
She's so right! Pick up a book!

119
00:11:35,403 --> 00:11:36,362
Those poor kids.

120
00:11:36,445 --> 00:11:40,408
You're one to talk! Weren't you just
on the verge of failing all your classes?!

121
00:11:41,575 --> 00:11:43,577
You and me, Chizu.

122
00:11:44,286 --> 00:11:48,499
We have to pay money to come here
and advance our education over the summer.

123
00:11:48,582 --> 00:11:51,919
They're the lucky ones who get to waltz in
and do that for free.

124
00:11:52,002 --> 00:11:55,047
I know we're here 'cause your single butt
needs a way to pass the time--

125
00:11:55,756 --> 00:11:57,591
Last I checked, you're single too!

126
00:12:01,220 --> 00:12:02,555
And you, Kazehaya?

127
00:12:04,140 --> 00:12:06,058
I'm taking summer classes too.

128
00:12:06,142 --> 00:12:09,019
- Oh cool! Same as me!
- Yeah, right. You're not going.

129
00:12:09,103 --> 00:12:10,813
So when shall we meet up?

130
00:12:11,439 --> 00:12:13,441
Speakin' of which,
we gettin' together soon?

131
00:12:13,524 --> 00:12:14,608
Yeah, duh!

132
00:12:21,949 --> 00:12:23,868
It's summer vacation.

133
00:12:23,951 --> 00:12:27,747
All right, I'll see you in class.
I'll keep in touch, okay?

134
00:12:27,830 --> 00:12:29,165
M-- me too!

135
00:12:35,755 --> 00:12:39,800
But... I'm not sure
what to talk to him about.

136
00:12:41,719 --> 00:12:43,220
Don't think too hard about it.

137
00:12:43,304 --> 00:12:46,640
You could say, "I'm tired,"
"It's hot outside," or "I just woke up."

138
00:12:46,724 --> 00:12:47,892
Anything really.

139
00:12:47,975 --> 00:12:48,976
Just like that?

140
00:12:50,019 --> 00:12:52,521
I... I hope it won't bother him.

141
00:12:52,605 --> 00:12:54,190
No, no, no, no, no.

142
00:12:55,399 --> 00:12:57,610
Even though we've officially
become a couple,

143
00:12:57,693 --> 00:13:00,446
I still don't have a single clue
what the first step is.

144
00:13:00,529 --> 00:13:02,323
Man, I feel ya.

145
00:13:02,406 --> 00:13:06,577
For the most part, dating's really just
about spending a lot of time together.

146
00:13:07,077 --> 00:13:10,414
Going places together and being together.

147
00:13:10,498 --> 00:13:13,751
As long as it's just you two,
don't sweat the details.

148
00:13:13,834 --> 00:13:16,170
- I see.
- Oh!

149
00:13:16,253 --> 00:13:17,755
It's setting in.

150
00:13:17,838 --> 00:13:20,299
Sawako really does have a boyfriend now.

151
00:13:20,382 --> 00:13:21,258
I'm lonely.

152
00:13:21,342 --> 00:13:22,551
You're lonely?

153
00:13:22,635 --> 00:13:24,136
Mm-hmm. Course I am.

154
00:13:24,220 --> 00:13:25,638
Curse you, Kazehaya!

155
00:13:25,721 --> 00:13:27,640
I mean, I am still happy for you, but...

156
00:13:28,265 --> 00:13:29,809
I'm so glad!

157
00:13:29,892 --> 00:13:33,312
Wait! Maybe this means
we can do things like this.

158
00:13:33,395 --> 00:13:34,772
Or even like that!

159
00:13:35,314 --> 00:13:38,150
We can see each other all the time
because it's summer.

160
00:13:38,234 --> 00:13:39,068
Yay!

161
00:13:40,319 --> 00:13:43,197
Hey, Chizu, Ayane... I love you.

162
00:13:43,280 --> 00:13:45,783
I love you too! Always and forever!

163
00:13:46,700 --> 00:13:48,661
Wait a second.

164
00:13:48,744 --> 00:13:52,456
When you two get together,
something is bound to happen eventually.

165
00:13:52,540 --> 00:13:55,042
I mean, you are a couple now.

166
00:13:55,125 --> 00:13:57,670
- Huh?
- Huh? Wait, I don't follow.

167
00:13:59,004 --> 00:14:01,549
When you're alone together,
it's only natural.

168
00:14:03,759 --> 00:14:05,553
You'll hold hands.

169
00:14:06,136 --> 00:14:08,138
Then you'll cuddle up.

170
00:14:09,348 --> 00:14:10,850
And kiss.

171
00:14:12,601 --> 00:14:13,727
Hold hands?

172
00:14:14,645 --> 00:14:15,646
Cuddle up?

173
00:14:18,190 --> 00:14:19,775
Kiss?!

174
00:14:24,947 --> 00:14:26,240
No, thank you!

175
00:14:26,323 --> 00:14:29,827
All of this is way more
than I can handle right now, I'm sorry!

176
00:14:29,910 --> 00:14:32,872
Chill. It's not a big deal.

177
00:14:33,372 --> 00:14:34,373
Don't be mean.

178
00:14:35,374 --> 00:14:36,876
Oh, all right.

179
00:14:36,959 --> 00:14:39,128
All these new feelings are totally normal,

180
00:14:39,211 --> 00:14:41,755
but I get why
they'd be a little overwhelming.

181
00:14:41,839 --> 00:14:42,715
Really?!

182
00:14:44,049 --> 00:14:45,926
I mean, of course.

183
00:14:46,468 --> 00:14:50,556
Oh, that reminds me, you still haven't
told us how your date went the other day.

184
00:14:50,639 --> 00:14:54,977
- Yeah! We want all the details!
- Right. The date was...

185
00:14:57,354 --> 00:14:58,355
- Huh?
- Huh?

186
00:14:59,148 --> 00:15:00,941
We planetarium-ed.

187
00:15:01,025 --> 00:15:03,944
I gave his gift to him.
But first, we bento-ed.

188
00:15:04,028 --> 00:15:05,571
- Huh?
- What?

189
00:15:06,572 --> 00:15:09,158
Hey, uh, what just happened?

190
00:15:09,241 --> 00:15:11,076
I don't have a clue.

191
00:15:36,936 --> 00:15:37,770
I'm sorry.

192
00:15:38,395 --> 00:15:42,024
I've kept you out longer
than I should have. Let's head back.

193
00:15:54,453 --> 00:15:57,164
After that, we walked home.

194
00:15:57,247 --> 00:16:00,334
With enough space between us
to fit a third person.

195
00:16:00,417 --> 00:16:02,086
Just like always.

196
00:16:04,630 --> 00:16:06,090
Aw, that's my girl.

197
00:16:06,173 --> 00:16:08,676
You've decided to attend
summer classes again, have you?

198
00:16:08,759 --> 00:16:09,760
Such a scholar!

199
00:16:09,843 --> 00:16:13,138
Huh! But kiddo, it's your summer vacation.

200
00:16:13,222 --> 00:16:15,140
Why not shake things up a little, huh?

201
00:16:15,224 --> 00:16:17,393
Like, I don't know,
inviting some friends over?

202
00:16:17,476 --> 00:16:19,520
How about Chizu or Ayane?

203
00:16:19,603 --> 00:16:20,771
What a good idea!

204
00:16:20,854 --> 00:16:23,357
- Girls have all the fun at this age.
- I wonder...

205
00:16:23,440 --> 00:16:27,069
-Is it time for me to tell Mom and Dad?
- ...invite your other friends too.

206
00:16:28,779 --> 00:16:30,280
Um, I uh...

207
00:16:30,864 --> 00:16:31,699
- Um?
- Um?

208
00:16:32,992 --> 00:16:34,410
So awkward!

209
00:16:37,705 --> 00:16:41,041
How do other girls
have this conversation with their parents?

210
00:16:42,584 --> 00:16:45,379
Maybe I should've asked Ayane for advice.

211
00:16:51,593 --> 00:16:53,387
I'll keep in touch.

212
00:16:55,347 --> 00:16:57,016
What'll we talk about?

213
00:16:57,099 --> 00:16:59,018
How often will you text?

214
00:16:59,101 --> 00:17:02,187
Can I text you sometimes too?

215
00:17:02,271 --> 00:17:05,482
If I message you out of the blue,
would it bug you?

216
00:17:05,566 --> 00:17:06,984
And what about summer break?

217
00:17:07,776 --> 00:17:09,695
You asked me out last time.

218
00:17:10,320 --> 00:17:12,448
So is it my turn to ask you out?

219
00:17:14,450 --> 00:17:17,911
Being in a relationship
sends my brain into overdrive.

220
00:17:21,707 --> 00:17:23,709
Oh, it's Kazehaya!

221
00:17:27,296 --> 00:17:31,216
THIS IS MARU

222
00:17:33,719 --> 00:17:37,139
MARU-CHAN IS SO CUTE

223
00:17:37,222 --> 00:17:38,640
SENDING

224
00:17:40,601 --> 00:17:41,977
Summer break.

225
00:17:43,604 --> 00:17:46,148
It's been... a whole year...

226
00:17:48,025 --> 00:17:51,153
since I started thinking
about Kazehaya like this.

227
00:17:53,363 --> 00:17:57,743
But now, I think about him
a lot more than I did back then.

228
00:17:59,244 --> 00:18:02,206
So much that it kinda hurts.

229
00:18:06,794 --> 00:18:08,962
SUMMER CLASSES
MODERN LIT, ENGLISH, MATH

230
00:18:13,008 --> 00:18:16,178
- I'm so tired!
- We've got English next.

231
00:18:16,261 --> 00:18:19,264
Did you see Joe?
He had a fat stack of printouts.

232
00:18:19,348 --> 00:18:20,182
For real?

233
00:18:21,767 --> 00:18:24,019
- Hey, Ayane.
- Uh?

234
00:18:24,103 --> 00:18:26,647
There's something I need to ask you about.

235
00:18:26,730 --> 00:18:27,564
Uh, what's up?

236
00:18:28,232 --> 00:18:32,986
Do you think it'd be appropriate
if I asked Kazehaya out after school?

237
00:18:33,070 --> 00:18:34,822
Maybe we could...

238
00:18:34,905 --> 00:18:35,823
Oh!

239
00:18:36,323 --> 00:18:38,700
What are you talking about?
Of course it's fine!

240
00:18:38,784 --> 00:18:40,244
Now go get 'im!

241
00:18:44,373 --> 00:18:45,249
Kuronuma.

242
00:18:48,502 --> 00:18:50,921
- Um, what if...
- Hm?

243
00:18:51,004 --> 00:18:54,925
What if, after school today,
we studied together at the library?

244
00:18:55,008 --> 00:18:56,426
Mmm, sounds good.

245
00:18:58,679 --> 00:19:01,723
She always takes everything so seriously.

246
00:19:03,350 --> 00:19:06,270
Oh well... typical Sawako.

247
00:19:06,353 --> 00:19:08,397
Ayane!

248
00:19:10,107 --> 00:19:12,192
That's a little familiar, don't you think?

249
00:19:12,276 --> 00:19:15,863
But guys are supposed to call girls
by their first names, aren't they?

250
00:19:16,405 --> 00:19:17,406
Maybe.

251
00:19:17,489 --> 00:19:19,950
But you called Sawako "Sadako," right?

252
00:19:23,036 --> 00:19:26,498
I'm just glad that it happened
before I started to like her.

253
00:19:28,041 --> 00:19:28,959
Hang on...

254
00:19:29,042 --> 00:19:32,004
- Do you call her Sadako on purpose?
- Uh--

255
00:19:34,256 --> 00:19:37,759
Well, I have lots of reasons.

256
00:19:39,178 --> 00:19:42,598
But don't you worry about it,
I only say it with love.

257
00:19:42,681 --> 00:19:44,474
Yeah, of course you do.

258
00:19:45,309 --> 00:19:47,144
Uh-oh! Next period's about to start.

259
00:19:47,227 --> 00:19:49,021
Bye!

260
00:19:50,397 --> 00:19:51,732
It's gonna be fine!

261
00:20:01,575 --> 00:20:05,787
It's over!
School's finally out, Yano-chin!

262
00:20:06,538 --> 00:20:09,499
- Where's Sawako?
- She went to the bathroom.

263
00:20:09,583 --> 00:20:11,543
Then, I'll go too! Hm?

264
00:20:13,170 --> 00:20:16,924
- About Sawako. Today, she's...
- Hm?

265
00:20:21,386 --> 00:20:24,598
I'm trying to wear my uniform
like the other girls do.

266
00:20:25,599 --> 00:20:29,603
Wait... something still isn't right.

267
00:20:32,814 --> 00:20:34,566
Oh yeah, the button.

268
00:20:38,153 --> 00:20:41,240
There! I undid my top button
just like the other girls!

269
00:20:42,241 --> 00:20:44,368
How does it look? Does it look good?

270
00:20:44,451 --> 00:20:45,744
A-- am I cute?!

271
00:20:47,204 --> 00:20:50,666
I mean, a single button
can't hurt, can it?

272
00:20:51,333 --> 00:20:55,128
Summer vacation
is not an excuse to get carried away.

273
00:20:55,212 --> 00:20:58,882
So remember
to conduct yourselves with propriety.

274
00:20:59,758 --> 00:21:03,303
It's fine!
One button won't ruin my conduct!

275
00:21:03,929 --> 00:21:06,348
I might be overthinking things a bit.

276
00:21:06,974 --> 00:21:10,143
Hey, Kuronuma!

277
00:21:12,271 --> 00:21:15,565
Yeah, so Yoshida and Yano said
they were gonna go on and head out.

278
00:21:15,649 --> 00:21:16,566
Huh?

279
00:21:17,192 --> 00:21:19,027
I didn't get to see Chizu at all!

280
00:21:19,111 --> 00:21:21,655
I bet leaving home early
was her plan all along.

281
00:21:21,738 --> 00:21:22,614
Oh!

282
00:21:23,657 --> 00:21:26,285
Your button's undone.

283
00:21:27,744 --> 00:21:31,164
Oh! Yeah, it is!
It's kind of hot today, so I must've...

284
00:21:31,999 --> 00:21:34,418
I'm so embarrassed!

285
00:21:34,501 --> 00:21:36,670
I guess it didn't look good
on me after all!

286
00:21:37,254 --> 00:21:41,425
There's absolutely no way I can tell him
I undid it on purpose!

287
00:21:53,061 --> 00:21:55,897
Please, don't look too closely.

288
00:21:57,941 --> 00:21:59,526
Stay just like that.

289
00:22:02,654 --> 00:22:04,823
I'm really sorry, Kazehaya.

290
00:22:07,284 --> 00:22:11,163
For some reason,
I'm just not myself at the moment.

291
00:22:19,254 --> 00:22:22,382
I want to spend more time with you.

292
00:22:23,383 --> 00:22:26,720
I want... to get closer...

293
00:22:28,764 --> 00:22:29,765
to you.

294
00:22:36,355 --> 00:22:38,190
Left field! Heads up!

295
00:22:40,692 --> 00:22:43,070
Look,
the baseball team's practicing.

296
00:22:44,738 --> 00:22:47,574
Kazehaya's behaving
like everything's normal.

297
00:22:51,703 --> 00:22:55,082
Oh, I'm sorry. I'm moving slow.

298
00:22:55,165 --> 00:22:59,002
Uh-- No, it's not you.
I was the one walking too fast. I'm sorry.

299
00:22:59,086 --> 00:23:01,380
Uh, no, it was me, I'm sure!

300
00:23:02,005 --> 00:23:05,217
I end up walking behind you,
whenever I start looking at you.

301
00:23:05,967 --> 00:23:06,885
Oh.

302
00:23:06,968 --> 00:23:09,638
It's hard to look at you
if I'm next to you.

303
00:23:12,015 --> 00:23:13,475
What did I say?!

304
00:23:17,729 --> 00:23:20,565
I couldn't help but notice
that you look different today.

305
00:23:21,066 --> 00:23:23,068
- Huh?
- Your uniform.

306
00:23:23,693 --> 00:23:25,695
Oh! Does it look funny?

307
00:23:25,779 --> 00:23:27,739
Uh--No, of course not.

308
00:23:27,823 --> 00:23:29,741
Hang on.

309
00:23:29,825 --> 00:23:33,745
If that's all you were worried about,
you should've just said something to me.

310
00:23:33,829 --> 00:23:36,456
Sorry, I'm kind of shy.

311
00:23:44,381 --> 00:23:46,007
I want to be with you.

312
00:23:47,050 --> 00:23:48,677
I want to be next to you.

313
00:23:49,469 --> 00:23:51,221
I want us to be close.

314
00:23:52,139 --> 00:23:53,390
Is that weird?

315
00:23:54,433 --> 00:23:57,769
It'll be fine.
All these new feelings are totally normal,

316
00:23:57,853 --> 00:24:00,105
but I get why
they'd be a little overwhelming.

317
00:24:16,288 --> 00:24:17,205
Could I

318
00:24:18,415 --> 00:24:20,625
hold your hand for a bit?

319
00:24:54,242 --> 00:24:55,327
Oh...

320
00:24:57,037 --> 00:24:58,914
Uh... sorry!

321
00:25:00,707 --> 00:25:03,376
I... messed up!

322
00:25:07,088 --> 00:25:10,175
He noticed. I know he did.

323
00:25:12,677 --> 00:25:15,847
Um, sorry! My mistake!

324
00:25:16,389 --> 00:25:17,599
I didn't mean...

325
00:25:17,682 --> 00:25:18,683
I just wanted...

326
00:25:19,392 --> 00:25:23,146
I... I'm sorry for trying to touch you.

327
00:25:23,730 --> 00:25:27,651
You were just acting the same way
you always do, and...

328
00:25:28,693 --> 00:25:30,904
...and I... I was the only...

329
00:25:32,614 --> 00:25:34,115
I'm so embarrassed.

330
00:25:37,994 --> 00:25:39,704
Please don't hate me.

331
00:25:55,053 --> 00:25:56,638
Same as always, huh?

332
00:26:06,856 --> 00:26:09,025
Do I look like
I'm acting normal?

333
00:27:16,426 --> 00:27:17,844
Sawako?

334
00:27:22,515 --> 00:27:24,392
M-- Mom?

335
00:27:28,855 --> 00:27:30,357
I... let go?

336
00:27:32,233 --> 00:27:34,402
Are... you on your way home?

337
00:27:36,029 --> 00:27:36,863
Yeah.

338
00:27:38,239 --> 00:27:40,909
I haven't told my mom about Kazehaya yet.

339
00:27:40,992 --> 00:27:42,160
She doesn't know.

340
00:27:43,495 --> 00:27:45,288
It's a tricky subject.

341
00:27:45,372 --> 00:27:48,291
I know I shouldn't be embarrassed. But...

342
00:27:49,334 --> 00:27:51,670
This is so rude to her and Kazehaya.

343
00:27:53,421 --> 00:27:55,674
Nice to meet you.

344
00:27:55,757 --> 00:27:57,717
My name is Shota Kazehaya.

345
00:27:57,801 --> 00:27:59,552
I'm in the same class as Kuronuma.

346
00:28:00,387 --> 00:28:03,139
I also happen to be going steady
with her at the moment.

347
00:28:03,223 --> 00:28:04,391
It's great to meet you.

348
00:28:04,974 --> 00:28:05,892
Oh, dear!

349
00:28:07,268 --> 00:28:08,353
Kazehaya!

350
00:28:11,815 --> 00:28:13,483
Um... Hey, Mom?

351
00:28:13,566 --> 00:28:16,027
I would also like to introduce him!

352
00:28:16,111 --> 00:28:17,153
This is Kazehaya!

353
00:28:17,237 --> 00:28:18,780
He's in the same class as me!

354
00:28:18,863 --> 00:28:21,282
In addition to that, we are also dating!

355
00:28:21,366 --> 00:28:23,284
Yes, I just heard.

356
00:28:24,369 --> 00:28:27,580
We've been classmates for a while.
Ever since first year.

357
00:28:28,331 --> 00:28:33,461
Also, because of Kazehaya's support,
I like school now.

358
00:28:33,545 --> 00:28:35,755
It's really, really fun
to go to my classes.

359
00:28:39,342 --> 00:28:41,469
It's also because he was there

360
00:28:41,553 --> 00:28:44,639
that Ayane, Chizu, and I
managed to become friends.

361
00:28:48,268 --> 00:28:52,355
That's not it.
Truth is, Kuronuma did it all on her own.

362
00:28:55,150 --> 00:28:56,443
Thank you so much.

363
00:28:56,526 --> 00:28:59,612
And it is such a pleasure
to finally meet you, Kazehaya.

364
00:28:59,696 --> 00:29:02,657
We're having sukiyaki
for dinner tonight.

365
00:29:02,741 --> 00:29:03,575
Huh?

366
00:29:03,658 --> 00:29:05,285
Sukiyaki, you sillies!

367
00:29:05,368 --> 00:29:08,621
Why don't you come
and have dinner with us, Kazehaya?

368
00:29:10,582 --> 00:29:12,959
Only if you want to. No pressure.

369
00:29:13,042 --> 00:29:16,921
Uh... I'd love to. I'll let my parents know.

370
00:29:18,548 --> 00:29:19,924
- Sawako.
- Huh?

371
00:29:20,508 --> 00:29:23,094
Why don't you give your father a call
and let him know?

372
00:29:25,054 --> 00:29:26,264
It should be you.

373
00:29:28,475 --> 00:29:29,350
Mm.

374
00:29:30,435 --> 00:29:34,272
I guess... Mom must've already noticed.

375
00:29:35,857 --> 00:29:38,943
She can tell
I regret not telling her myself

376
00:29:39,027 --> 00:29:40,737
before we ran into each other.

377
00:29:41,362 --> 00:29:44,365
Yeah. She's the one that
I told you about the other day.

378
00:29:45,408 --> 00:29:48,286
I'm gonna go have dinner with her family.

379
00:29:49,037 --> 00:29:53,416
Me too.
I'll tell him. I'll tell my father.

380
00:29:59,714 --> 00:30:02,467
Hello, hello, Sawako!
Is something the matter?

381
00:30:03,760 --> 00:30:07,013
Um, there's something I wanted to say.

382
00:30:07,096 --> 00:30:08,640
Oh. Well, let's hear it.

383
00:30:08,723 --> 00:30:11,392
And don't worry,
I'll be home soon!

384
00:30:11,935 --> 00:30:12,769
So I've...

385
00:30:13,311 --> 00:30:15,396
I've begun seeing someone at school.

386
00:30:16,564 --> 00:30:20,235
Oh, and... he's coming over today.

387
00:30:25,782 --> 00:30:28,660
He's... he's silent!

388
00:30:34,999 --> 00:30:37,961
- Oh-oh-oh-oh-oh-oh!
- It's going to be okay!

389
00:30:38,044 --> 00:30:41,005
Your father is in for a long day.

390
00:30:41,089 --> 00:30:43,633
Oh-oh-oh-oh-oh-oh-oh-oh-oh!

391
00:30:46,386 --> 00:30:49,514
My, my!
Who's this strapping young man with you?

392
00:30:49,597 --> 00:30:52,433
Could this be your boyfriend?!

393
00:30:52,517 --> 00:30:53,518
That's right!

394
00:30:54,394 --> 00:30:56,813
- Nice to meet you.
- What a gentleman!

395
00:30:56,896 --> 00:31:01,276
Your father's definitely
going to faint!

396
00:31:02,694 --> 00:31:05,738
I'm... so nervous.

397
00:31:08,825 --> 00:31:10,159
Is it just me?

398
00:31:11,619 --> 00:31:14,038
Hey, Sawa! Who's your new friend?

399
00:31:14,122 --> 00:31:14,956
Hello, sir!

400
00:31:15,039 --> 00:31:18,418
- Oh my! Who's that with you, Sawako?
- Nice to meet you.

401
00:31:19,002 --> 00:31:21,504
Oh!
Bringing your boyfriend over?

402
00:31:21,588 --> 00:31:22,672
Nice to meet you!

403
00:31:22,755 --> 00:31:26,593
- Well, he's quite the catch, isn't he?!
- Right?

404
00:31:26,676 --> 00:31:30,805
Kazehaya, thanks so much.
Are you okay? Sorry about this.

405
00:31:30,889 --> 00:31:32,432
Huh? Oh, uh...

406
00:31:33,099 --> 00:31:37,186
Relax. I'm doing great.
Maybe a little nervous...

407
00:31:37,270 --> 00:31:39,063
It's not hard to tell,

408
00:31:39,147 --> 00:31:41,733
you're obviously very close
with all your neighbors.

409
00:31:42,358 --> 00:31:45,320
And I'm really excited
to finally meet your mom and dad.

410
00:31:45,945 --> 00:31:46,946
Huh?

411
00:31:47,030 --> 00:31:50,825
I, uh... I think I'm actually
a lot more nervous than I'm letting on.

412
00:31:52,452 --> 00:31:54,412
Maybe the most I've ever been!

413
00:31:55,747 --> 00:31:58,249
Dad... Mom...

414
00:31:59,417 --> 00:32:03,171
this person right here... is the one I love.

415
00:32:03,713 --> 00:32:07,008
And this... is what he's like.

416
00:32:10,303 --> 00:32:13,389
Come on, you kids,
let's get a move on.

417
00:32:13,473 --> 00:32:14,432
Yes, ma'am.

418
00:32:15,892 --> 00:32:19,938
It all felt so natural...
falling in love.

419
00:32:20,772 --> 00:32:22,649
And wanting to hold hands.

420
00:32:25,276 --> 00:32:29,322
There are things that I have to say
and things that I want to say.

421
00:32:30,365 --> 00:32:34,035
I never thought... not for a moment,

422
00:32:34,118 --> 00:32:37,038
that I would ever develop feelings
that I'd want to keep

423
00:32:38,539 --> 00:32:39,832
all to myself.

424
00:32:56,307 --> 00:32:57,934
Dad, this is Kazehaya.

425
00:33:01,562 --> 00:33:04,315
Kazehaya, this is my father.

426
00:33:05,108 --> 00:33:06,359
Good to meet you, sir.

427
00:33:06,859 --> 00:33:11,114
I'm one of your daughter's classmates.
My name's Shota Kazehaya.

428
00:33:13,282 --> 00:33:16,202
So here he is! Shota Kazehaya.

429
00:33:16,285 --> 00:33:17,954
The boy I mentioned on the phone.

430
00:33:19,080 --> 00:33:21,207
He's the one I've officially begun dating.

431
00:33:24,419 --> 00:33:27,380
Wasn't I clear?

432
00:33:27,463 --> 00:33:30,008
You were just
supposed to bring a friend over.

433
00:33:30,091 --> 00:33:32,051
I don't think you were that specific.

434
00:33:32,135 --> 00:33:34,971
I remember you saying
she should bring "someone" over.

435
00:33:35,054 --> 00:33:38,850
Obviously, I meant she should've
brought home a girl, damn it!

436
00:33:38,933 --> 00:33:41,185
But this is...
I cannot deny what's before me!

437
00:33:41,269 --> 00:33:44,564
This person is obviously your boyfriend!

438
00:33:46,941 --> 00:33:48,401
"Obviously"?

439
00:33:48,484 --> 00:33:50,903
"My boyfriend"?!

440
00:33:52,739 --> 00:33:54,407
Thank you, Dad!

441
00:33:54,490 --> 00:33:56,117
What are you talking about?

442
00:33:56,200 --> 00:33:59,662
The thing you just said.
I don't hear it very often.

443
00:33:59,746 --> 00:34:02,123
Seriously, you really
think they're dating?

444
00:34:02,206 --> 00:34:05,501
- Nuh-uh, there's no way.
- I don't know what kinda rumor you heard.

445
00:34:07,003 --> 00:34:10,631
I never imagined there would come a day
when I'd hear you say that to me.

446
00:34:15,928 --> 00:34:19,057
I'm embarrassed, but... I am happy.

447
00:34:19,640 --> 00:34:21,142
- Aw!
- Uh-huh!

448
00:34:23,811 --> 00:34:26,230
I...

449
00:34:26,314 --> 00:34:28,066
Sir, I promise to treat her well.

450
00:34:28,733 --> 00:34:31,027
Ahhhhh!

451
00:34:31,652 --> 00:34:34,238
Yoko! My grinding stone, where is it?

452
00:34:38,951 --> 00:34:40,328
Um, Dad?

453
00:34:42,371 --> 00:34:45,708
I picked this up from our neighbor,
Ikeda, on my way home.

454
00:34:48,252 --> 00:34:50,171
- Time to dig in.
- Wait, what?

455
00:34:50,254 --> 00:34:52,840
What? Are you too good
for Mr. Ikeda's fish?

456
00:34:52,924 --> 00:34:56,719
- Is that what you're telling me now?
- Thank you for the food.

457
00:34:58,304 --> 00:35:00,973
Hoo! That's great. Props to Mr. Ikeda.

458
00:35:01,057 --> 00:35:03,142
Exactly. His fish is always the best.

459
00:35:03,226 --> 00:35:05,812
Is he...
trying to be a good host?

460
00:35:05,895 --> 00:35:10,108
It might've sounded better to say,
"I prepared this fish for you myself."

461
00:35:10,191 --> 00:35:14,112
Hmm.
No flaws in his chopstick technique.

462
00:35:14,195 --> 00:35:17,573
And he remembered to say,
"Thanks for the food."

463
00:35:17,657 --> 00:35:19,534
All right, come on now, dear.

464
00:35:19,617 --> 00:35:22,495
I'm sure the sashimi's great,
but maybe you should change?

465
00:35:22,578 --> 00:35:23,955
Sawako too.

466
00:35:24,789 --> 00:35:26,415
Oh, but I...

467
00:35:27,583 --> 00:35:28,668
Go on ahead.

468
00:35:31,254 --> 00:35:33,548
I... I'll be right back.

469
00:35:34,048 --> 00:35:35,883
You too, darling. Go on!

470
00:35:35,967 --> 00:35:37,718
Yeah. You're right.

471
00:35:40,805 --> 00:35:43,266
- Here you go.
- Uh-- Thank you.

472
00:35:43,891 --> 00:35:47,478
- I'm really sorry for all the trouble.
- No, it's fine.

473
00:35:47,562 --> 00:35:50,898
It's just that
my husband loves Sawako dearly.

474
00:35:51,816 --> 00:35:54,152
Yeah, I figured that out pretty quick.

475
00:35:54,944 --> 00:35:59,657
It was really easy to see.
There are so many people who care for her.

476
00:36:02,243 --> 00:36:07,415
Uh-huh. Kazehaya, did we happen to talk
over the phone for a bit during Christmas?

477
00:36:07,498 --> 00:36:08,499
Oh yeah, I remember!

478
00:36:08,583 --> 00:36:11,210
That's what I thought.
You were such a big help.

479
00:36:11,294 --> 00:36:12,253
Thank you so much.

480
00:36:14,547 --> 00:36:16,883
She's a very logical girl, you know.

481
00:36:17,717 --> 00:36:18,551
Because of that,

482
00:36:18,634 --> 00:36:22,388
she does have a bit of a tendency
to put her feelings on the back burner.

483
00:36:23,347 --> 00:36:26,767
That one time, however,
she was the one who brought it up.

484
00:36:26,851 --> 00:36:28,895
She must've really wanted to go.

485
00:36:30,688 --> 00:36:33,733
It made me so happy
to hear her tell me herself.

486
00:36:35,151 --> 00:36:37,695
She's been smiling a lot lately.

487
00:36:38,863 --> 00:36:41,240
I bet she's having a lot of fun.

488
00:36:43,409 --> 00:36:45,411
You should know, that girl,

489
00:36:45,494 --> 00:36:48,539
she might look shy,
but she does go after what she wants.

490
00:36:48,623 --> 00:36:51,918
- Have you had your first fight yet?
- No, hasn't happened yet.

491
00:36:52,543 --> 00:36:55,254
If it does,
I'd just wanna make up though.

492
00:36:55,338 --> 00:36:59,217
By the way,
do you remember when you became official?

493
00:36:59,300 --> 00:37:00,968
Uh, since the school festival.

494
00:37:01,052 --> 00:37:02,553
So who asked who out first...

495
00:37:02,637 --> 00:37:04,805
- Yoko!
- ...and what did they say?

496
00:37:04,889 --> 00:37:07,767
- Stop! Enough questions!
- Ah, shoot.

497
00:37:07,850 --> 00:37:10,561
And here I thought
I'd find out before Sawako got back.

498
00:37:11,395 --> 00:37:15,775
Uh? What's wrong, dear?
Why did you get your winter hat out?

499
00:37:18,277 --> 00:37:22,031
There was a mix-up at Christmas,
and my dad ended up with the hat instead.

500
00:37:23,115 --> 00:37:26,702
Yeah, you see this? This hat?

501
00:37:26,786 --> 00:37:29,872
Sawako made it just for me.

502
00:37:29,956 --> 00:37:33,501
Kazehaya, I bet you don't
have anything like this.

503
00:37:33,584 --> 00:37:37,713
Sorry but I do.

504
00:37:37,797 --> 00:37:39,131
You've gotta be kidding?!

505
00:37:39,715 --> 00:37:41,759
Wait, Dad,
why are you wearing that right now?

506
00:37:41,842 --> 00:37:43,594
Well I... I, uh...

507
00:37:44,178 --> 00:37:48,015
Why don't you wait with Sawako in her room
while I finish up the sukiyaki?

508
00:37:48,099 --> 00:37:49,642
- Huh?!
- Hey!

509
00:37:49,725 --> 00:37:52,353
Don't you think it's a little early
to be letting him go up there?

510
00:37:52,436 --> 00:37:55,398
Maybe you should've thought of that
before taking up the whole kitchen

511
00:37:55,481 --> 00:37:57,942
to sharpen your knife and delay dinner!

512
00:37:58,859 --> 00:38:00,111
Um, shall we?

513
00:38:00,194 --> 00:38:02,405
Yeah. Sure.

514
00:38:05,241 --> 00:38:07,785
You keep that door open,
you hear me?

515
00:38:07,868 --> 00:38:10,079
Yes! I'll keep that door open, sir!

516
00:38:10,162 --> 00:38:14,000
I'm sorry for always putting you
in such awkward situations.

517
00:38:14,083 --> 00:38:15,668
Why? I don't mind.

518
00:38:17,586 --> 00:38:21,424
It's better to feel awkward now,
'cause when else will I get the chance?

519
00:38:24,427 --> 00:38:27,054
Knowing there's someone
who likes me this way

520
00:38:27,638 --> 00:38:29,348
makes me feel so safe.

521
00:38:30,641 --> 00:38:35,313
'Til now, only my parents' words
of encouragement gave me that feeling.

522
00:38:35,396 --> 00:38:38,691
Like when they'd say,
"It'll be okay," or "We love you."

523
00:38:39,650 --> 00:38:42,611
- And here we are.
- Um, thanks.

524
00:38:43,904 --> 00:38:46,324
My world's gotten
a little bigger now.

525
00:38:46,407 --> 00:38:51,537
I get that same feeling
from Chizu, Ayane, and Kazehaya too.

526
00:38:55,708 --> 00:38:59,045
Please, feel free to have a seat.

527
00:38:59,128 --> 00:39:00,588
What's the matter?

528
00:39:01,589 --> 00:39:03,841
Sorry. Just nerves, I guess.

529
00:39:04,467 --> 00:39:07,678
I'm about as nervous as I was
when I first met your parents.

530
00:39:12,516 --> 00:39:14,352
That's from
the school festival.

531
00:39:14,435 --> 00:39:18,939
- Uh, yeah. I got it from Chizu.
- Oh, cool.

532
00:39:20,107 --> 00:39:21,609
Look at that smile.

533
00:39:39,585 --> 00:39:42,171
She's a very logical girl,
you know.

534
00:39:44,507 --> 00:39:46,509
I-- I'm sorry.

535
00:39:49,387 --> 00:39:51,138
Please don't hate me!

536
00:39:52,848 --> 00:39:57,061
But how could I ever...
ever come to hate you?

537
00:40:18,165 --> 00:40:22,086
Something I haven't been able
to figure out, no matter how hard I try,

538
00:40:22,169 --> 00:40:24,004
is how to act in front of you.

539
00:40:24,839 --> 00:40:26,799
Am I making mistakes?

540
00:40:26,882 --> 00:40:28,259
Am I doing things right?

541
00:40:29,844 --> 00:40:31,554
I was scared.

542
00:40:31,637 --> 00:40:34,223
Worried it would all
suddenly come crashing down.

543
00:40:35,015 --> 00:40:37,518
That's why I wanted time to pass quickly.

544
00:40:39,270 --> 00:40:42,314
To finally reach a point
where things felt okay.

545
00:40:44,525 --> 00:40:47,736
You know, mistakes aren't
the end of the world.

546
00:40:49,071 --> 00:40:49,947
It's okay.

547
00:40:56,328 --> 00:40:57,163
Yeah.

548
00:40:58,873 --> 00:41:00,082
Everything's okay.

549
00:41:03,043 --> 00:41:04,378
I love you.

550
00:41:05,463 --> 00:41:06,797
Sukiyaki time, kiddos!

551
00:41:06,881 --> 00:41:09,383
Argh! Why are you sitting
so close to her?!

552
00:41:09,467 --> 00:41:11,844
- I'm sorry, it just sorta happened!
- Just sorta happened?!

553
00:41:11,927 --> 00:41:14,763
- I'm the one who came over and sat down!
- No, that can't be true!

554
00:41:17,516 --> 00:41:19,894
Help yourself
to some meat, Kazehaya.

555
00:41:19,977 --> 00:41:22,438
- Yes, ma'am.
- Whoa there, kid!

556
00:41:22,521 --> 00:41:25,441
The only thing
I've seen you pick up so far is the meat!

557
00:41:25,524 --> 00:41:27,443
- Eat your vegetables!
- Y-- yes, sir.

558
00:41:27,526 --> 00:41:31,405
- You need fiber too!
- He's making an effort!

559
00:41:31,489 --> 00:41:35,326
Meat, veggies, meat, veggies,
veggies, meat, veggies!

560
00:41:35,409 --> 00:41:37,244
Sir! Everything here's...

561
00:41:37,328 --> 00:41:40,039
Kazehaya's also doing his best
to make conversation.

562
00:41:40,122 --> 00:41:41,415
Settle down, dear.

563
00:41:42,082 --> 00:41:46,170
He always tries his best to make sure
that I feel safe and comfortable.

564
00:41:47,671 --> 00:41:50,382
I want to stop my worries
from getting in the way

565
00:41:51,634 --> 00:41:54,178
and be faithful to Kazehaya's feelings.

566
00:41:58,224 --> 00:41:59,725
That's who I want to be.

567
00:42:13,531 --> 00:42:16,534
Um... here. Mom said to give you this.

568
00:42:16,617 --> 00:42:19,870
- Hey, buster! Who you callin' "Mom"?!
- You're right, I'm sorry!

569
00:42:20,579 --> 00:42:22,873
I can't finish all that.

570
00:42:22,957 --> 00:42:24,583
- Sit down.
- Uh-- uh-- okay.

571
00:42:29,255 --> 00:42:31,215
So, tell me, why Sawako?

572
00:42:31,757 --> 00:42:35,302
A guy like you
has got to have options, right?

573
00:42:38,097 --> 00:42:39,223
No, sir.

574
00:42:39,306 --> 00:42:41,183
Your daughter's the only one for me.

575
00:42:41,267 --> 00:42:44,019
You're lucky
you don't look anything like this!

576
00:42:44,103 --> 00:42:47,690
- 'Cause otherwise I would never approve!
- Uh... No, I'm sorry.

577
00:42:50,109 --> 00:42:52,528
How is Sawako performing in school?

578
00:42:53,112 --> 00:42:54,780
She's a really good student.

579
00:42:54,863 --> 00:42:58,158
And she does her fair share
of work for the student council too.

580
00:42:58,993 --> 00:43:02,621
It seems like she's always
havin' a good time.

581
00:43:03,789 --> 00:43:04,957
Hmm.

582
00:43:07,251 --> 00:43:11,130
Don't worry about trying to grow up
into some extraordinary person.

583
00:43:11,964 --> 00:43:14,508
If you're happy and healthy,
that's enough.

584
00:43:19,346 --> 00:43:22,933
My Sawako has never been very forthcoming
when it comes to her emotions.

585
00:43:23,017 --> 00:43:24,518
Even as a little girl.

586
00:43:24,602 --> 00:43:26,395
But all that has changed.

587
00:43:26,478 --> 00:43:30,149
It's clear, even to me,
she is finally having fun.

588
00:43:31,025 --> 00:43:35,654
Chizu, Ayane, and yes, even you,
are probably a big part of why that is.

589
00:43:37,740 --> 00:43:38,741
I thank you.

590
00:43:45,831 --> 00:43:48,208
Uh, thank you for today.

591
00:43:48,876 --> 00:43:51,587
Oh, you're welcome.
Thanks for having me for dinner.

592
00:43:52,755 --> 00:43:55,257
Maybe you can come to my house next time.

593
00:43:55,341 --> 00:43:57,092
- Really?
- Uh-huh.

594
00:43:59,261 --> 00:44:01,096
'Cause I...

595
00:44:08,687 --> 00:44:11,023
Never mind. Later!

596
00:44:11,106 --> 00:44:12,858
Uh, get home safe!

597
00:44:17,821 --> 00:44:21,867
I'm sorry. You were just acting
the same way you always do.

598
00:44:27,581 --> 00:44:30,626
I bet... she doesn't realize it...

599
00:44:33,045 --> 00:44:34,546
but I feel the same way.

600
00:44:38,008 --> 00:44:39,718
When I'm with you, Kuronuma,

601
00:44:41,178 --> 00:44:43,472
I just don't know what to do with myself.

602
00:44:49,812 --> 00:44:54,733
FROM ME TO YOU: KIMI NI TODOKE

603
00:45:02,449 --> 00:45:03,867
It's August.

604
00:45:03,951 --> 00:45:07,246
Summer classes are almost done.
And then come Obon.

605
00:45:08,205 --> 00:45:10,207
Maru, down!

606
00:45:10,290 --> 00:45:12,751
Are you okay, Kuronuma? I'm sorry.

607
00:45:12,835 --> 00:45:14,586
Ah! You're so big!

608
00:45:14,670 --> 00:45:16,088
- Come on, Maru!
- You remember me?

609
00:45:16,171 --> 00:45:18,298
- You're such a good puppy, aren't you?
- Heel! Sit!

610
00:45:20,467 --> 00:45:22,511
When the Obon holidays begin,

611
00:45:22,594 --> 00:45:25,013
you know the end of summer
is around the corner.

612
00:45:25,097 --> 00:45:27,307
And so is the end of summer break.

613
00:45:27,975 --> 00:45:30,811
I know I suggested
doing our homework together,

614
00:45:30,894 --> 00:45:32,604
but now that I think about it,

615
00:45:32,688 --> 00:45:34,815
you've probably already finished
your homework, right?

616
00:45:34,898 --> 00:45:39,027
I have. But I do still have
lots of other things that I can study!

617
00:45:39,111 --> 00:45:40,320
I called it!

618
00:45:41,613 --> 00:45:46,076
Even so, I would've wanted
to come to your house anyway, Kazehaya.

619
00:45:49,705 --> 00:45:52,040
Today, I'm extra nervous.

620
00:45:52,124 --> 00:45:55,210
This'll be my first time
going to Kazehaya's place.

621
00:45:55,294 --> 00:45:58,422
I wonder what his family will be like?

622
00:45:58,922 --> 00:46:00,841
I hope I don't make a mistake.

623
00:46:01,759 --> 00:46:05,053
I want to do my best
to be pleasant and cheerful.

624
00:46:05,137 --> 00:46:08,766
Hopefully, I don't forget to smile
and make a good first impression.

625
00:46:08,849 --> 00:46:11,143
I don't want to make them uncomfortable.

626
00:46:11,685 --> 00:46:16,607
MARTINEZ

627
00:46:16,690 --> 00:46:18,358
WIND SPORTS

628
00:46:22,613 --> 00:46:23,614
I'm home!

629
00:46:24,656 --> 00:46:27,493
Wait, does your family run a shop?
That's so interesting.

630
00:46:27,576 --> 00:46:30,829
- I never would've imagined.
- Uh-- You mean, I never told you this?

631
00:46:32,664 --> 00:46:35,417
Shota! There's a spot
on the glass next to you.

632
00:46:35,501 --> 00:46:38,796
- Do you mind getting it?
- Uh... Oh, you mean here?

633
00:46:38,879 --> 00:46:42,674
Uh, you'll have to forgive me.
My mom's pretty prickly.

634
00:46:42,758 --> 00:46:44,968
What did you just call me? Oh--

635
00:46:45,928 --> 00:46:49,473
Is this Sawako?
Sawako Kuronuma?

636
00:46:50,057 --> 00:46:53,310
Thank you for coming by.
I've heard lots about you.

637
00:46:53,393 --> 00:46:55,854
I'm Shota's mom. Nice to meet you.

638
00:46:57,147 --> 00:47:01,026
They're so similar.
Their aura is exactly the same.

639
00:47:01,652 --> 00:47:04,279
So that's why
you were cleaning your room.

640
00:47:04,363 --> 00:47:07,241
Mom, stop!
Let's not go there, please.

641
00:47:07,783 --> 00:47:11,161
So this... is Kazehaya's mom.

642
00:47:11,912 --> 00:47:15,249
I'm Sawako Kuronuma!

643
00:47:15,874 --> 00:47:17,626
Uh-- It's nice to meet you!

644
00:47:17,709 --> 00:47:20,128
Oh, I totally forgot to smile!

645
00:47:20,712 --> 00:47:21,755
Lighten up!

646
00:47:21,839 --> 00:47:24,967
If you get any stiffer,
you might end up snapping like a twig!

647
00:47:25,050 --> 00:47:26,844
S... stiff?

648
00:47:27,427 --> 00:47:29,680
My, Sawako, your hair...

649
00:47:30,389 --> 00:47:32,432
Was I supposed to tie it up?

650
00:47:32,516 --> 00:47:35,853
You've got such beautiful locks.
So vibrant and shiny.

651
00:47:36,687 --> 00:47:38,939
What a blessing it must be
to have a daughter.

652
00:47:39,022 --> 00:47:42,776
To be honest with you, I often wish
I'd given birth to a little girl.

653
00:47:42,860 --> 00:47:43,986
Jeez, my bad!

654
00:47:44,069 --> 00:47:48,907
It's really Kazehaya's mom!

655
00:47:51,451 --> 00:47:53,954
Oh, right. Um, this is for you.

656
00:47:54,037 --> 00:47:57,708
It's a really good red-bean jelly
that my whole family likes a lot.

657
00:47:57,791 --> 00:48:03,005
Wow, really? That's lovely.
Thank you so much. Oh, Sawako...

658
00:48:03,088 --> 00:48:06,550
There's no need for all this formality.
You really didn't have to!

659
00:48:06,633 --> 00:48:09,928
You might not be able to tell,
but my mom's really excited

660
00:48:10,012 --> 00:48:12,264
'cause she loves red-bean jelly. Nice job!

661
00:48:12,347 --> 00:48:14,725
Hey, knock it off!
Don't give it away!

662
00:48:15,350 --> 00:48:17,394
I'm sorry my son is so difficult.

663
00:48:17,477 --> 00:48:19,688
I'm sorry my mom is so difficult.

664
00:48:26,111 --> 00:48:29,323
Well, what are you waiting for?
Don't just stand there!

665
00:48:29,406 --> 00:48:31,158
Feel free to come on in.

666
00:48:31,241 --> 00:48:33,911
Just so you know, she's always like this.

667
00:48:33,994 --> 00:48:35,787
Oh-- Just like what, huh?

668
00:48:36,997 --> 00:48:40,250
- Am I taking these boxes over there?
- That's right.

669
00:48:40,334 --> 00:48:42,544
Do you mind? Since you're here, after all.

670
00:48:46,798 --> 00:48:51,094
So that's how he was brought up.
It's what made him who he is today.

671
00:48:54,514 --> 00:48:58,018
Sorry we spent
so much time talking before going in.

672
00:48:58,101 --> 00:49:01,813
Huh? Oh no, it's fine.
I'm glad I got to meet your mom.

673
00:49:01,897 --> 00:49:04,441
That's good. Man, what a relief.

674
00:49:04,524 --> 00:49:08,070
- Oh, was there something worrying you?
- Yeah, of course, I was worried.

675
00:49:08,779 --> 00:49:11,281
It's really important to me
that you like us.

676
00:49:16,578 --> 00:49:18,413
Uh, thanks for having me over.

677
00:49:19,331 --> 00:49:22,376
So what are your dad
and brother up to today?

678
00:49:23,043 --> 00:49:27,255
- They're playing baseball.
- I see. Little league, I'm guessing?

679
00:49:29,675 --> 00:49:31,259
Come on in.

680
00:49:40,769 --> 00:49:42,854
This is Kazehaya's room!

681
00:49:43,939 --> 00:49:46,858
Just pick any spot you like,
and make yourself comfortable.

682
00:49:46,942 --> 00:49:49,569
- I'm gonna go get us some tea, okay?
- Uh, I'll help.

683
00:49:49,653 --> 00:49:53,573
It's fine, don't worry about it.
Just relax and flip through a book or two.

684
00:49:58,870 --> 00:50:02,499
Wow, what a huge collection!
He's got so many CDs too!

685
00:50:02,582 --> 00:50:05,502
This is where he studies!
He sleeps on a bed!

686
00:50:07,004 --> 00:50:09,506
So this... is where he lives!

687
00:50:11,299 --> 00:50:14,428
I bet everything in this room
is a special thing he likes.

688
00:50:15,429 --> 00:50:19,016
Oh, I really wanna do
a full, in-depth tour of the place.

689
00:50:19,099 --> 00:50:22,102
But I shouldn't. Not without asking first.

690
00:50:23,729 --> 00:50:26,815
I'm ba-- Duh!
You still haven't sat down yet?

691
00:50:27,399 --> 00:50:30,360
I might've snuck a little peek
at your books, and your CDs,

692
00:50:30,444 --> 00:50:33,655
and all other little aspects
of your personal life that are in here.

693
00:50:33,739 --> 00:50:36,992
I'm not trying to hide those! If I were,
I wouldn't have invited you here.

694
00:50:37,075 --> 00:50:38,410
Oh! Is that true?

695
00:50:38,994 --> 00:50:41,371
Was there anything in particular
that caught your interest?

696
00:50:41,455 --> 00:50:42,539
Whoa!

697
00:50:45,667 --> 00:50:47,419
I haven't organized these yet.

698
00:50:47,502 --> 00:50:49,963
I don't mind. Is it okay if I look?

699
00:50:50,547 --> 00:50:52,799
It's a bit embarrassing
but I won't stop you.

700
00:50:52,883 --> 00:50:55,510
I'll just look for a little bit.

701
00:50:56,845 --> 00:51:01,767
- Is this from the test of courage?
- Oh yeah, it is! That was a fun night.

702
00:51:01,850 --> 00:51:05,103
So that must be what it felt like
down on earth for everyone else.

703
00:51:05,187 --> 00:51:06,188
"Down on earth"?

704
00:51:06,855 --> 00:51:10,233
Ah, if we ever do this again,
I'd know exactly how to give everyone

705
00:51:10,317 --> 00:51:12,569
an even bigger scare this time around.

706
00:51:12,652 --> 00:51:15,197
- That's if it happens again.
- Huh?

707
00:51:15,280 --> 00:51:17,783
If it does,
we'd be walking the course together.

708
00:51:18,366 --> 00:51:20,494
- I'm going to walk it?
- Well, yeah, duh!

709
00:51:21,286 --> 00:51:22,746
Together with you?

710
00:51:23,914 --> 00:51:25,248
You don't want to?

711
00:51:25,332 --> 00:51:28,877
I do. I'd like that.

712
00:51:32,464 --> 00:51:35,258
Sorry... I just...

713
00:51:42,140 --> 00:51:43,391
Can I tell you something?

714
00:51:44,476 --> 00:51:48,605
Back then, on that night...
I already liked you.

715
00:51:50,440 --> 00:51:52,609
Huh?! What do you mean, you liked me?

716
00:51:52,692 --> 00:51:54,277
What do you mean by that?

717
00:51:54,361 --> 00:51:56,780
And what does that mean
for us right now?

718
00:51:56,863 --> 00:51:59,950
Mm-mmm. Actually, never mind!
Don't worry about it!

719
00:52:00,033 --> 00:52:01,785
You don't have to tell me anything!

720
00:52:05,455 --> 00:52:09,292
I like when people know how... to have fun.

721
00:52:11,294 --> 00:52:13,839
You think... I'm like that?

722
00:52:14,589 --> 00:52:15,882
Yeah. I do.

723
00:52:18,301 --> 00:52:19,136
Always.

724
00:52:28,770 --> 00:52:30,397
I can't sit this close!

725
00:52:31,398 --> 00:52:32,691
I'm gonna go study.

726
00:52:34,234 --> 00:52:38,321
Right now, he's... so close to me.

727
00:52:40,740 --> 00:52:44,911
When I first started school,
I never imagined this would happen.

728
00:52:45,412 --> 00:52:47,581
MATH II

729
00:52:48,540 --> 00:52:50,375
Uh... when you...

730
00:52:51,751 --> 00:52:53,587
when you called me by my name.

731
00:52:56,173 --> 00:52:58,216
When you called me "Sawako."

732
00:52:59,384 --> 00:53:00,760
Sawako.

733
00:53:00,844 --> 00:53:02,846
Sawako Kuronuma. Right?

734
00:53:09,936 --> 00:53:11,855
Sawa... ko.

735
00:53:16,234 --> 00:53:19,362
Not "Kuronuma." And not "Sadako."

736
00:53:21,031 --> 00:53:23,366
I want to fit the name "Sawako."

737
00:53:24,451 --> 00:53:26,494
None of it really matters anymore.

738
00:53:27,913 --> 00:53:30,582
As long as I treasure
the words he just said...

739
00:53:32,500 --> 00:53:33,335
forever.

740
00:53:36,087 --> 00:53:39,591
I'm not looking from behind
or from the side.

741
00:53:39,674 --> 00:53:42,177
We see each other face-to-face.

742
00:53:42,260 --> 00:53:44,596
And we both feel the same way.

743
00:53:51,561 --> 00:53:52,938
I'm so glad.

744
00:53:56,191 --> 00:53:58,693
I had no idea
that you knew back then.

745
00:53:59,319 --> 00:54:03,114
When I called you by your first name.

746
00:54:04,824 --> 00:54:06,785
You know, after the party?

747
00:54:08,703 --> 00:54:09,871
- Huh?
- Wha--

748
00:54:10,455 --> 00:54:13,875
Uh? Wait, which time
are you talking about, then?

749
00:54:14,459 --> 00:54:16,294
Back when we first spoke.

750
00:54:16,378 --> 00:54:19,130
We were standing in front of
the flowers, remember?

751
00:54:19,214 --> 00:54:21,132
You asked if I was Sawako Kuronuma.

752
00:54:21,216 --> 00:54:24,219
Oh, right!
I guess I technically did!

753
00:54:24,886 --> 00:54:28,139
After what party though?
You mean the sports festival?

754
00:54:29,683 --> 00:54:30,976
I don't understand.

755
00:54:33,478 --> 00:54:36,731
At the after-party!
I called you by your name on the stairs!

756
00:54:38,108 --> 00:54:39,359
I said "Sawako."

757
00:54:39,943 --> 00:54:43,321
Why am I giving it away now?

758
00:54:44,406 --> 00:54:47,617
I didn't know my feelings for you
began such a long time ago.

759
00:54:48,660 --> 00:54:50,662
Me... me neither.

760
00:54:56,251 --> 00:54:57,961
Sawako.

761
00:54:59,671 --> 00:55:02,257
Sho... Shota.

762
00:55:05,844 --> 00:55:08,221
Oh my!

763
00:55:09,681 --> 00:55:11,266
Oh man!

764
00:55:11,349 --> 00:55:15,020
- How am I supposed to study like this?
- I can't...

765
00:55:17,897 --> 00:55:20,525
- Oh hey! Looks like my mom's calling me!
- Huh?

766
00:55:21,276 --> 00:55:22,360
Hi, what's up?

767
00:55:23,528 --> 00:55:24,362
Yeah.

768
00:55:25,238 --> 00:55:26,072
Huh?

769
00:55:29,951 --> 00:55:32,954
Sorry you got dragged into
doing errands with me, Kuronuma.

770
00:55:33,038 --> 00:55:36,791
Would you two do me a huge favor
and go get a little ice cream for Tota?

771
00:55:36,875 --> 00:55:39,377
Huh? Oh, I don't mind at all.

772
00:55:39,461 --> 00:55:43,298
- I mean, we were supposed to study...
- Yeah, but I mean...

773
00:55:44,215 --> 00:55:47,093
Well, we weren't gonna
be able to stay focused anyway.

774
00:55:47,177 --> 00:55:49,012
S'pose you're right.

775
00:55:50,638 --> 00:55:54,017
That's right. I haven't met
his father or younger brother yet.

776
00:55:55,060 --> 00:55:57,145
I wonder what kind of people they are?

777
00:55:58,646 --> 00:56:01,983
So, uh, your younger brother,
what's his name?

778
00:56:02,067 --> 00:56:04,486
Tota. Take "to"
from the word "transparent,"

779
00:56:04,569 --> 00:56:06,863
and "ta" from my name, and you get "Tota."

780
00:56:06,946 --> 00:56:09,240
Tota!
Do you look like each other?

781
00:56:09,324 --> 00:56:11,201
Yeah.
He's basically a smaller me.

782
00:56:11,284 --> 00:56:12,786
A smaller you?!

783
00:56:13,453 --> 00:56:17,040
- And what about your father?
- Huh? My father?

784
00:56:17,123 --> 00:56:19,292
We, uh... Hmm...

785
00:56:19,376 --> 00:56:21,461
Actually, I'm not sure if we look alike.

786
00:56:22,128 --> 00:56:24,672
Nah, I don't think that
there's much resemblance at all.

787
00:56:24,756 --> 00:56:28,176
But, then again, Pin and my mom
are both constantly going on about

788
00:56:28,259 --> 00:56:30,136
how similar my father and I look.

789
00:56:30,220 --> 00:56:31,554
So you do look alike?

790
00:56:31,638 --> 00:56:34,808
Uh-- Well-- No.
I really don't think we do.

791
00:56:34,891 --> 00:56:37,477
- The Kazehaya of the past...
- He's a coach, isn't he?

792
00:56:37,560 --> 00:56:40,021
- Yeah.
- ...and the Kazehaya of the future!

793
00:56:42,065 --> 00:56:43,525
Stretching time!

794
00:56:44,025 --> 00:56:49,572
One, two, three,
four, five, six, seven, eight!

795
00:56:49,656 --> 00:56:52,033
Two, two, three, four...

796
00:56:52,117 --> 00:56:56,996
Did you see that TV show
about ghosts last night? It was so scary!

797
00:56:57,080 --> 00:57:00,542
What? No way! You know
there's no such thing as ghosts, right?

798
00:57:00,625 --> 00:57:01,751
Yes, there is!

799
00:57:01,835 --> 00:57:05,422
There was this skinny girl in
a white dress, walking through the grass.

800
00:57:05,505 --> 00:57:07,424
And she had super long hair.

801
00:57:07,507 --> 00:57:11,803
- Nah! Well, I like curvy girls better.
- I don't remember if she had curves.

802
00:57:12,387 --> 00:57:15,682
But, she was walking around
with what looked like a plastic bag.

803
00:57:15,765 --> 00:57:18,393
Whoa!
Just like that girl over there!

804
00:57:21,062 --> 00:57:23,022
Exactly like that!

805
00:57:28,695 --> 00:57:29,612
Whoa!

806
00:57:38,037 --> 00:57:41,124
Hey!
You can't just skip the exercises!

807
00:57:43,668 --> 00:57:44,669
Tota.

808
00:57:48,673 --> 00:57:50,758
Well, there he is.
This is my little brother.

809
00:57:51,843 --> 00:57:54,512
He... he's like a mini Kazehaya!

810
00:57:55,221 --> 00:57:57,515
Hi there! I-- it's nice to meet you!

811
00:57:57,599 --> 00:58:00,560
- Uh, I'm Sawako Ku--
- So, like, are you Shota's woman?

812
00:58:01,227 --> 00:58:04,898
-"Woman"?!
- Hey, what's going on?

813
00:58:04,981 --> 00:58:06,983
- That's Shota's woman.
- Really?

814
00:58:07,734 --> 00:58:09,903
- Ow!
- Might've said too much.

815
00:58:09,986 --> 00:58:11,738
What? Isn't she your woman?

816
00:58:11,821 --> 00:58:13,865
- Wait, is she not?
- What's going on.

817
00:58:13,948 --> 00:58:16,284
We are together,
but don't call her my "woman."

818
00:58:16,367 --> 00:58:18,119
- So it is true!
- Oh, you were right!

819
00:58:18,203 --> 00:58:20,413
- You're so right!
- Hey, nice catch, Shota!

820
00:58:20,497 --> 00:58:22,499
That's enough outta you guys.

821
00:58:23,708 --> 00:58:26,419
Well, I'm Sawako Kuronuma.

822
00:58:27,128 --> 00:58:29,130
It-- it's very nice to meet you.

823
00:58:32,717 --> 00:58:33,551
Sawako!

824
00:58:33,635 --> 00:58:35,637
Just like that?

825
00:58:38,806 --> 00:58:40,975
You look like a ghost!

826
00:58:42,435 --> 00:58:45,188
- She's flat as a board.
- Yeah, you got that right.

827
00:58:45,271 --> 00:58:46,856
- She got nothin'.
- Nothin' at all.

828
00:58:48,274 --> 00:58:51,069
I can't lie.
Not much going on around here.

829
00:58:51,152 --> 00:58:52,570
Tota, shut up!

830
00:58:57,325 --> 00:58:59,911
Look over there. Here comes my father.

831
00:59:03,706 --> 00:59:06,960
It's Kazehaya... of the future!

832
00:59:11,798 --> 00:59:14,008
The future?!

833
00:59:14,092 --> 00:59:16,970
Where's Martinez?
Didn't you bring him with you?

834
00:59:17,053 --> 00:59:19,722
- Oh.
- He was fast asleep.

835
00:59:19,806 --> 00:59:20,890
He was what?

836
00:59:20,974 --> 00:59:23,268
An animal lover?

837
00:59:23,351 --> 00:59:26,604
Well, I hope you at least
brought the ice cream manjū I like.

838
00:59:26,688 --> 00:59:30,483
- I did. No need to get fussy.
- Just hurry up and hand it over.

839
00:59:35,530 --> 00:59:38,241
Hmm? And who are you supposed to be?

840
00:59:38,825 --> 00:59:41,035
This is Sawako Kuronuma, my classmate.

841
00:59:42,245 --> 00:59:44,539
And my girlfriend.

842
00:59:45,456 --> 00:59:46,958
Girlfriend, huh?

843
00:59:48,710 --> 00:59:51,671
I believe I was asking
the young lady who she was.

844
00:59:51,754 --> 00:59:53,798
Why were you the one who answered?

845
00:59:53,881 --> 00:59:55,008
He's right!

846
00:59:55,592 --> 00:59:59,012
Dad, I'm gonna need you
to mind your tone.

847
00:59:59,095 --> 01:00:01,431
I-- I apologize for the delay.

848
01:00:01,514 --> 01:00:04,517
If you would please allow me
the honor of introducing myself.

849
01:00:05,101 --> 01:00:07,020
Show me what you got!

850
01:00:07,103 --> 01:00:08,521
Nice to meet you.

851
01:00:08,605 --> 01:00:12,233
Many know me as, um,
uh, a classmate of Shota's.

852
01:00:12,317 --> 01:00:14,319
They call me Sawako Kuronuma.

853
01:00:14,402 --> 01:00:17,363
In Kitamachi, within Kitahoro,
is where I live.

854
01:00:17,447 --> 01:00:20,575
Father works for the city,
while my mother is a housewife.

855
01:00:20,658 --> 01:00:24,162
At school, I have taken on the duty
of tending to the herb garden.

856
01:00:24,245 --> 01:00:29,876
When I have a day off, um, the activities
I often enjoy include various crafts,

857
01:00:29,959 --> 01:00:32,045
like baking sweets and drawing...

858
01:00:32,962 --> 01:00:35,590
More recently,
I have started listening to rakugo CDs

859
01:00:35,673 --> 01:00:38,676
while diving into
extensive research about ghost stories.

860
01:00:39,260 --> 01:00:42,013
At the moment, I am not a member
of any of the extracurricular clubs

861
01:00:42,096 --> 01:00:43,264
at my high school.

862
01:00:43,348 --> 01:00:45,725
However, should a rakugo club come around,

863
01:00:45,808 --> 01:00:48,144
boy-oh-boy, would I want to partake
in a club like that.

864
01:00:48,227 --> 01:00:49,270
That's enough.

865
01:00:49,354 --> 01:00:53,149
What I really want to know is
are you sure you're eating properly?

866
01:00:53,232 --> 01:00:54,984
I've never seen such skinny arms.

867
01:00:55,068 --> 01:00:58,446
I try to eat three meals a day
to 80% fullness each time.

868
01:00:58,529 --> 01:01:00,365
- Well, try to eat more.
- Sir!

869
01:01:00,448 --> 01:01:01,532
How 'bout exercise?

870
01:01:02,116 --> 01:01:05,119
I-- I maintain my strength
by running once every week.

871
01:01:05,203 --> 01:01:08,247
Oh, and I do
some aerobic exercise every day too.

872
01:01:08,331 --> 01:01:11,876
Good. Sawako, which item
will you choose to consume?

873
01:01:11,959 --> 01:01:14,087
Huh? Oh, I haven't thought about it yet.

874
01:01:14,170 --> 01:01:17,048
What do you have to think about?
The manjū' s right there.

875
01:01:17,131 --> 01:01:18,466
- It's the best!
- Okay!

876
01:01:19,092 --> 01:01:22,553
- So what do you think? Good, right?
- Yes! It's good!

877
01:01:22,637 --> 01:01:23,554
Exactly.

878
01:01:28,726 --> 01:01:29,977
Here we go!

879
01:01:30,061 --> 01:01:35,149
One, two! One, two, three, four.
One, two! One, two, three...

880
01:01:35,233 --> 01:01:39,445
Your dad, he's very much
like a typical father, isn't he?

881
01:01:39,946 --> 01:01:43,658
I think the difference
between him and my dad is dignity.

882
01:01:43,741 --> 01:01:44,575
Dignity?

883
01:01:45,284 --> 01:01:50,081
I guess that's one way to put it,
but I always thought he was a bad father.

884
01:01:50,164 --> 01:01:51,082
Really?

885
01:01:51,165 --> 01:01:53,334
Hey, you there!
That's enough chit-chat!

886
01:01:53,418 --> 01:01:55,461
All right, pick up the pace!

887
01:01:55,545 --> 01:01:58,005
Oh, he's talking to the kids.

888
01:01:58,089 --> 01:02:00,800
Or is he doing it on purpose? Maybe.

889
01:02:09,934 --> 01:02:12,812
You know, Kuronuma, I think he likes you.

890
01:02:20,403 --> 01:02:21,821
He likes you, Sawako.

891
01:02:22,613 --> 01:02:27,034
Mom, Tota, Dad, and Maru...

892
01:02:27,827 --> 01:02:29,912
The whole Kazehaya family.

893
01:04:24,402 --> 01:04:27,655
- Huh? Are you heading home now?
- Yeah.

894
01:04:27,738 --> 01:04:30,867
Perfect timing!
Here. Inari sushi from my mom!

895
01:04:31,367 --> 01:04:32,952
Mmm, thanks.

896
01:04:34,579 --> 01:04:36,956
You're just gonna
eat that right here?!

897
01:04:37,039 --> 01:04:38,457
Well, yeah, I'm hungry.

898
01:04:39,083 --> 01:04:42,086
I mean,
I guess your practice did go kinda late.

899
01:04:42,587 --> 01:04:44,755
And you? How was the review class?

900
01:04:44,839 --> 01:04:47,133
I feel like
my brain's gonna explode.

901
01:04:47,216 --> 01:04:49,677
You studied more
for the entrance exams, right?

902
01:04:49,760 --> 01:04:53,222
Well, yeah... duh! Of course I did.
I really wanted to get in.

903
01:04:53,306 --> 01:04:56,475
My brother... already graduated, y'know?

904
01:04:56,559 --> 01:05:00,813
Huh?! Hold on. Why do you think
I wanted to get into Kitahoro?

905
01:05:01,397 --> 01:05:04,317
Because it's the school
my brother graduated from, right?

906
01:05:06,402 --> 01:05:09,071
It's because that's where
you were going, Ryu!

907
01:05:11,657 --> 01:05:12,533
Just think.

908
01:05:12,617 --> 01:05:16,203
Let's say you got into Kitahoro,
and I went somewhere else.

909
01:05:16,287 --> 01:05:18,080
We'd be going to different schools.

910
01:05:18,164 --> 01:05:20,207
If our teams met at baseball prelims,

911
01:05:20,291 --> 01:05:23,377
then am I... supposed to root
against your school?

912
01:05:23,461 --> 01:05:25,755
I couldn't bring myself to do that!

913
01:05:25,838 --> 01:05:29,967
'Cause I wanna...
I wanna cheer for you, Ryu.

914
01:05:31,177 --> 01:05:33,095
And no one else but you!

915
01:05:34,430 --> 01:05:35,473
Chizuru...

916
01:05:35,556 --> 01:05:38,976
What's wrong with you?
Don't look at me! You big dumb idiot!

917
01:05:39,060 --> 01:05:40,102
I'm going home.

918
01:05:44,899 --> 01:05:46,901
Hey, the heck are you doing?

919
01:05:49,028 --> 01:05:49,862
Thank you.

920
01:05:54,075 --> 01:05:56,494
You're a big giant colossal idiot!

921
01:06:04,251 --> 01:06:05,169
Idiot.
